WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.894 --> 00:00:19.596
Soon Valjean's eyes grew accustomed to the darkness.

2
00:00:19.597 --> 00:00:26.226
He had entered the sewer from a grate along the street, and the faint light from above penetrated the tunnel.

3
00:00:26.227 --> 00:00:30.063
Valjean laid Marius down while he rested for a moment.

4
00:00:30.064 --> 00:00:35.956
Then he slung the wounded man across his back again and set off through the tunnel.

5
00:00:35.957 --> 00:00:42.956
Marius was gravely ill and unconscious. Perhaps Valjean had no chance of saving him.

6
00:00:42.957 --> 00:00:50.877
Valjean had been walking for about half an hour when he saw his shadow in front of him. Puzzled, he turned around.

7
00:00:50.878 --> 00:00:59.781
In the distance he saw some torchlight, and behind that some people were moving. Valjean stood with his back against the wall.

8
00:00:59.782 --> 00:01:04.860
He must escape from these people even though he did not know their identities.

9
00:01:04.861 --> 00:01:10.791
In fact, they were policemen who had been ordered to search the sewers for rebels.

10
00:01:10.792 --> 00:01:16.352
Luckily for Valjean, he could see the police better than they could see him.

11
00:01:16.353 --> 00:01:22.757
They had heard his footsteps, but now that he had stopped moving, they decided that nobody was there.

12
00:01:22.758 --> 00:01:29.875
Just to be sure, one policeman fired a shot in Valjean's direction. It hit the arch over his head.

13
00:01:29.876 --> 00:01:35.336
Valjean remained motionless until the men turned around and disappeared in the dark.

14
00:01:35.337 --> 00:01:39.400
Meanwhile another chase had been going on aboveground.

15
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:46.832
A policeman had been following a suspicious character, hoping that the man might lead him to a band of criminals.

16
00:01:46.833 --> 00:01:52.919
As they approached the docks on the Seine River, the man disappeared behind a rubbish pile.

17
00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:59.240
The policeman quickened his pace, but after passing the rubbish pile, he stopped in amazement.

18
00:01:59.241 --> 00:02:02.800
The man he'd been pursuing was nowhere to be seen.

19
00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:11.133
Then he noticed a grate covering a wide, dark opening. Unlike the one near the barricade, this grate was locked.

20
00:02:11.134 --> 00:02:19.641
"Of course!" said the policeman. "He went into the sewer. Somewhere he must have found a key to open the grate."

21
00:02:19.642 --> 00:02:28.292
After Valjean's encounter with the police, he continued to walk for hours with Marius on his back. He was very tired.

22
00:02:28.293 --> 00:02:32.918
When he came to a large air hole, he laid Marius on the ground.

23
00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:38.689
In the light, he could see that Marius was still breathing despite his terrible wounds.

24
00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:43.065
Valjean searched Marius' pockets and found a scrap of bread to eat.

25
00:02:43.066 --> 00:02:48.356
He also found the note with Marius' name and Monsieur Gillenormand's address.

26
00:02:48.357 --> 00:02:52.776
"Now I know who he is and where to take him," said Valjean.

27
00:02:52.777 --> 00:03:02.078
But at that moment, Valjean had no idea where they were. He pushed on and soon felt the stone under his feet replaced with mud.

28
00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:10.340
"This is like a swamp, but I can't go back," said Valjean. "Marius is dying, and I must press on."

29
00:03:10.341 --> 00:03:15.794
The water rose up to his armpits, and yet he still kept going forward.

30
00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:21.586
Valjean sank deeper and struggled to keep Marius' head above water.

31
00:03:21.587 --> 00:03:30.103
At last Valjean felt something solid under his feet. The path before him gradually sloped uphill and the water receded.

32
00:03:30.104 --> 00:03:35.499
When he reached a dry spot, Valjean sank to his knees, exhausted.

33
00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:43.055
But Valjean managed to stand once more. He had carried Marius only a hundred paces when he saw a wall.

34
00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:47.237
Valjean looked to his left and saw a light far away.

35
00:03:47.238 --> 00:03:48.785
"There's an opening!"

36
00:03:48.786 --> 00:03:55.642
Valjean no longer felt exhausted. He practically ran to the outlet, but then he stopped.

37
00:03:55.643 --> 00:04:03.808
It was covered with a grate, and a sturdy lock held it shut. Beyond the grate, Valjean could see docks and the river.

38
00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:12.379
"It's all over," said Valjean. "We're trapped in this place." He put his head in his hands and thought of Cosette.

39
00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:20.371
Suddenly someone laid a hand on Valjean's shoulder and said, "You want to split what's in this guy's pockets?"

40
00:04:20.372 --> 00:04:24.325
Valjean looked up and saw Thenardier standing before him.

41
00:04:24.326 --> 00:04:30.688
They gazed at each other for a moment, and Valjean realized that Thenardier did not recognize him.

42
00:04:30.689 --> 00:04:38.347
"You've obviously killed this guy and need to get out of here," Thenardier went on. "And I have a key to the grate."

43
00:04:38.348 --> 00:04:45.093
Valjean nodded, but said nothing as Thenardier busied himself searching Marius' pockets.

44
00:04:45.094 --> 00:04:52.180
"That old man is an odd fellow," Thenardier thought. "There's something strange going on here.

45
00:04:52.181 --> 00:04:59.260
I'm going to tear a strip from this young guy's coat. You never know when something like that will come in handy."

46
00:04:59.261 --> 00:05:05.903
Thenardier removed a few coins from Marius' pockets and kept them all, lying to Valjean.

47
00:05:05.904 --> 00:05:12.998
"He didn't have any money. Not much point in killing him, was there? Here, I'll let you out now."

48
00:05:12.999 --> 00:05:18.649
With that, he put the key in the lock and opened the grate for Valjean.

49
00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:24.982
"Good luck!" said Thenardier as he locked the grate again and disappeared inside the sewer.

50
00:05:24.983 --> 00:05:32.157
Valjean stood for a moment breathing in the fresh air. Then he carried Marius over to the docks.

51
00:05:32.158 --> 00:05:38.244
He dipped his hand into the river and let a few drops of water fall on Marius' face.

52
00:05:38.245 --> 00:05:42.212
The unconscious man stirred but did not open his eyes.

53
00:05:42.213 --> 00:05:49.674
Suddenly Valjean heard footsteps behind him. He turned and there stood Javert.

54
00:05:49.675 --> 00:05:54.633
It was Javert who had been pursing Thenardier until he disappeared into the sewer!

55
00:05:54.634 --> 00:06:00.314
"Who are you?" Javert asked the mud-covered man kneeling on the dock next to Marius.

56
00:06:00.315 --> 00:06:04.037
"Don't you recognize me? I'm Valjean."

57
00:06:04.038 --> 00:06:10.696
Javert stared into his eyes. "What are you doing here and who is this injured man?"

58
00:06:10.697 --> 00:06:16.942
"I've considered myself your prisoner since I gave you my address this morning," said Valjean.

59
00:06:16.943 --> 00:06:23.354
"Do with me what you will, but first help me carry this boy to his grandfather's house."

60
00:06:23.355 --> 00:06:30.100
Javert studied Marius' face. "He was in the barricade, wasn't he? His name is Marius."

61
00:06:30.101 --> 00:06:35.788
Valjean felt in Marius' pocket and pulled out the paper with his grandfather's address.

62
00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:39.489
"We must take him here, quickly before he dies."

63
00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:45.814
At Monsieur Gillenormand's house, a servant helped the two men carry Marius inside.

64
00:06:45.815 --> 00:06:52.963
As they got back into the carriage again, Valjean said, "Inspector Javert, grant me one more thing.

65
00:06:52.964 --> 00:06:55.981
Allow me to go home before you arrest me."

66
00:06:55.982 --> 00:07:02.973
"Fine," said Javert, "but only for a few minutes. I'll wait for you in the street."

67
00:07:02.974 --> 00:07:07.779
At his apartment building, Valjean headed upstairs with a heavy heart.

68
00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:13.648
His life was over now that Javert had caught him; he was going back to prison.

69
00:07:13.649 --> 00:07:19.640
But he needed to say good-bye to Cosette and tell her that he'd found Marius.

70
00:07:19.641 --> 00:07:23.946
On the landing Valjean paused to gaze out the window.

71
00:07:23.947 --> 00:07:30.878
He leaned out further and looked up and down the street. To his amazement, Javert was gone!

72
00:07:30.879 --> 00:07:36.027
Javert walked slowly away from Valjean's house and headed for the river.

73
00:07:36.028 --> 00:07:41.283
He had been in turmoil ever since Valjean had spared his life that morning.

74
00:07:41.284 --> 00:07:48.401
Javert felt something new and horrible penetrating his soul: admiration for a convict.

75
00:07:48.402 --> 00:07:54.188
Here was a criminal who was compassionate, who took pity rather than vengeance.

76
00:07:54.189 --> 00:07:58.259
Surely this man could not really exist, but he did.

77
00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:02.596
Javert had reached the river now, his thoughts torturing him.

78
00:08:02.597 --> 00:08:10.180
His whole belief system—what was right, what was wrong—had been turned upside down by Jean Valjean.

79
00:08:10.181 --> 00:08:16.592
He felt that he had failed somehow, that it would be impossible to continue doing his job.

80
00:08:16.593 --> 00:08:21.816
Javert jumped into the river and was swept away by the current.
